      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "info",
          "title": "IFC to OpenUSD Converter",
          "paragraphs": [
            "IfcUSD bridges BIM and USD-based DCC pipelines by converting IFC building models into Pixar's OpenUSD format. It uses IfcOpenShell to read and tessellate IFC geometry, then writes <code>.usd</code>, <code>.usda</code>, or <code>.usdc</code> files through the OpenUSD Python bindings. The converter writes tessellated meshes as <code>UsdGeom.Mesh</code> prims while preserving the full IFC spatial hierarchy as USD <code>Xform</code> prims under <code>/IFC</code>.",
            "The workflow is geometry-first but metadata-rich: IFC identity (STEP id, GlobalId, class, name, tag, predefined type), property sets, quantity takeoffs, USD Preview Surface materials with diffuse/specular/opacity, face subsets, external texture references, unit assignments, and relationship metadata (spatial containers, aggregate parents, types, groups, layers, openings, and references) are all carried into the USD stage so downstream tools retain the full BIM context."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "features",
          "title": "What Gets Written",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "fas fa-shapes",
              "html": "Tessellated IFC products as <code>UsdGeom.Mesh</code> prims"
            },
            {
              "icon": "fas fa-sitemap",
              "html": "IFC spatial hierarchy as USD <code>Xform</code> prims under <code>/IFC</code>"
            },
            {
              "icon": "fas fa-paint-brush",
              "html": "USD Preview Surface materials, colors, opacity, and face subsets"
            },
            {
              "icon": "fas fa-image",
              "html": "External texture references from IFC surface-style data"
            },
            {
              "icon": "fas fa-database",
              "html": "IFC property sets and quantity takeoffs as USD attributes"
            },
            {
              "icon": "fas fa-project-diagram",
              "html": "Spatial containers, aggregates, types, groups, layers, openings"
            },
            {
              "icon": "fas fa-ruler-combined",
              "html": "USD stage unit metadata from the IFC unit assignment"
            }
          ]
        },
